    metric: Kendall tau_b vs p0  (|tau|->1 = fewer inversions = cleaner monotone)
================================================================================
  #sets = 1716
  tau(additive energy AE, p0) = +0.3929
  tau(spectral flatness SF, p0) = -0.3408   (expect NEGATIVE: flat spectrum -> low cover)
  tau(diff-set size |E-E|, p0) = -0.2398   (spread)
  tau(width max(E), p0)        = -0.1842

  p0-argmax set = (0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7)  p0=0.3272  (is it consecutive (0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7)?)
  AE-argmax set = (0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7)   SF-argmin set = (0, 1, 3, 4, 5, 6, 8, 9)

  strict discordant pairs (out of 1471470):
    AE (+): 405181 (27.5%)   SF (-): 484870 (33.0%)   |E-E| (+): 677169 (46.0%)
  => BEST single predictor by |tau|: additive energy (|tau|=0.3929)

